cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the TRIAD checklist or the audit procedure, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "triad-audit: a three-layer response integrity audit for deployability"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenyongjingg/triad-audit"
abstract: >-
  The audit checklist and the eight-step procedure from the manuscript
  "An Empirical Audit of an AI System's Evaluation Pipeline: A Deployed
  Guardrail's Reported Operating Point Is Produced by the Measurement
  Apparatus".  TRIAD is an audit
  procedure, not a detector: it reports whether a guardrail's reported
  operating point is produced by the evaluation apparatus rather than by the
  guardrail. This is a scaffold release -- the checklist, the procedure and
  the recorded numbers are transcribed from the manuscript; the code that
  produced them is not yet released.
keywords:
  - audit
  - evaluation validity
  - guardrail evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - measurement
